-- title:
--   Witt rigidity: Frobenius lifts commute with maps out of W(k)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ a perfect field of characteristic $p$ (perfectness being recorded by a `PerfectRing k p` instance). Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring, $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$, and let $O$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra; write $(\pi) =$ `Ideal.span {algebraMap 𝒪 O π}` for the ideal of $O$ generated by the image of $\pi$. Assume $O$ is Hausdorff for the $(\pi)$-adic filtration, i.e. $\bigcap_{n} (\pi)^n = 0$ in the sense of `IsHausdorff`, and that $p \in (\pi)$ as an element of $O$. Let $\mathrm{Fr} : O \to O$ be a ring homomorphism satisfying $\mathrm{Fr}(x) - x^p \in (\pi)$ for every $x \in O$, and let $\iota : W(k) \to O$ be any ring homomorphism from the ring of $p$-typical Witt vectors of $k$. The conclusion is the equality of ring homomorphisms $W(k) \to O$ given by $\mathrm{Fr} \circ \iota = \iota \circ F$, where $F =$ `WittVector.frobenius` is the Witt vector Frobenius.
--
--   This is the rigidity property of Witt vectors over a perfect field: a Frobenius lift on a $\pi$-adically separated algebra in which $p$ lies in $(\pi)$ automatically intertwines any map out of $W(k)$ with the Witt Frobenius, which is the uniqueness statement underlying the theory of strict $p$-rings and Teichmüller representatives. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where the Frobenius twist of the $W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})$-structure on formal modules over an unramified base has to be identified with $\sigma \circ \iota$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WittVector_ringHom_comp_eq_comp_frobenius_of_sub_pow_mem_of_isHausdorff.lean

